From 4de8e210b3bf58bbd41de4986b7b1d19e35220dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: adesh chaudhari <superbhel7@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 08:28:17 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] feat(frontend): wire the auth pages and add the missing
 admin login screen

YG-4.

LoginPage calls /api/auth/otp/request and carries the phone to OtpPage, which
verifies and stores the JWT. Both handle 429: OTP is capped at 5 per phone per
15 minutes with a 60s resend cooldown, so rate limiting will fire in testing.

AdminLoginPage is new and not in the plan. /api/auth/admin/login has always
existed but had no UI, which meant there was no way to obtain an ADMIN token
and therefore no way into /admin/* at all.

The plan allows prefilling the OTP box from devOtp. We deliberately do not:
it makes verification look staged, hides the wrong-OTP and rate-limit paths
from testing, and would change behaviour the moment SZ-6 turns mock mode off.
The code is shown in a dev-only notice instead, so testing stays quick.
